~ start
System: A busy sidewalk. Kael is cleaning the front door of his shop and notices the MC lingering.
Kael: You alright? You've been standing there staring at the window for a while.
- Just caught my reflection and it kind of ruined my mood. I hate how I look today.
    => kael_flaws
- I'm just over-analyzing everything I see in the glass. It's a hard habit to break.
    => kael_flaws

~ kael_flaws
Kael: I get it, but honestly? Your brain is probably seeing 'flaws' that literally no one else on this street is even noticing.
- I know, but it feels so real when I'm the one looking at it.
    => kael_body
- I guess I'm just looking for reasons to be hard on myself right now.
    => kael_body

~ kael_body
Kael: Try to just see it as a reflection of a person walking. It's just a body doing its job, getting you from A to B.
- Right. It's just a body. I don't have to love it to appreciate that it's working.
    => END
- I need to stop letting a piece of glass decide if I'm having a good day or not.
    => END